@* // PinFinder Spec using MudText component *@
@* <MudText Typo="Typo.h4">New PinFinder Classic Spec</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Release version 1.2.8</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User goes to pinfinder.intel.com web page</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">If you select “iTUFF Prober”, it will go to the specific SITE that is selected</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User is able to select another Site in 2nd drop down menu</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User types in a Lot</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[site_ituffs] table is queried for that site to get all of the search paths for that site</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Paths are searched and Operation Pull down is populated</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User selects an Operation</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[site_ituffs] table is queried for that site to get all of the search paths for that site</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Summary file list Pull down is populated</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User select a Summary (MIDAS file is included in this list)</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">User hits “Submit” (or happens right after a Summary is Chosen?)</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">iTuff Parser starts</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h6">iTuff tokens used for Lot / Part information:</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_lotid_Lot ID</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_prgnm_Test Program Name</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_packg_Package</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_prdct_Product</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_testertype_Tester Type</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">6_comnt_socfile_Socket File</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">5_lcode_Location Code / Operation</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">4_smrynam_Summary Name</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">4_sysid_Tester Name</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">4_tempr_Temperature</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">4_ldbid_ / _tiuid_Tiu ID</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">3_lsepUnit Separator</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">3_prtnm_Part Number</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">3_socket_Socket Number</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">3_curfbin_Function Bin (i.e. 301)</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">3_curibin_Interface Bin (i.e. 3)</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">2_visualid_Visual ID</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">2_trlot_ / 2_sstrlot_Sort Lot</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">2_trwafer_ / 2_sstrwafer_Sort Wafer</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">2_trxloc_ / 2_sstrxloc_Sort X location</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">2_tryloc_ / 2_sstryloc_Sort Y location</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h6">iTuff header is parsed to determine the “key” for the [pinfinder_config] table:</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Package_ID_Search_Text] Ex:6_packg_~~~</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Test_Program_Search_Text]</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Test_Program_Search_Text] Ex:6_prgnm_~~~</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Interface_Unit_ID_Search_Text] Ex:4_ldbid_~~~, 3_tiuid_~~~</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Tester] Ex:6_testertype_~~~</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[pinfinder_config] is queried to match the above conditions and returns the row containing the above fields as well as:</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Interface Unit Design ID]</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">[Manufactured Unit Design ID]</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">If no match is found, then the product isn’t configured properly and Error is returned</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">iTuff file is parsed and output (failing channels) stored on a JSON</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Call Trace to find out which failing test name prefix matches the user’s bin</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">If no match from Trace, determine which key words in the 2_tname field corresponds to the user’s bin(s)</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Read “BinTokens” JSON text file to look up the keys words for each bin</MudText>

<MudText Typo="Typo.h6">BinTokens JSON text file:</MudText>
<MudText Typo="Typo.body1">"8": "HWALARM,!DFF,cont,CONT,vcc,Cont,VCC,Vcc,shorts",</MudText>
